// Package gomockgen documents stateful fakes
// generated by the go-mockgen template for [mockery].
//
// The template is the file go-mockgen.templ in this directory
// (with its JSON schema go-mockgen.templ.schema.json).
// It generates the same public API as [go-mockgen] v2.1.1,
// so tests written for go-mockgen fakes work unchanged with the generated ones,
// and the go-mockgen documentation stays valid.
// The template is frozen: it gets compatibility fixes only, never new features.
//
// This package contains the example interface [Store] and its fake generated by the template:
// see [MockStore], its constructors [NewMockStore], [NewStrictMockStore], [NewMockStoreFrom]
// and per-method types like [StoreGetFunc] and [StoreGetFuncCall] for the generated API.
//
// # Naming
//
// All names are derived from mockery's structname option.
// Let S be the structname with a leading "Mock" trimmed.
// For an interface with a method M the template generates:
//
//   - the fake struct named structname (MockS) with a field MFunc per method;
//   - constructors NewMockS, NewStrictMockS and NewMockSFrom;
//   - per-method types SMFunc (hooks and call history) and SMFuncCall (one recorded call).
//
// go-mockgen names a fake by the title-cased interface name with an optional --prefix,
// which corresponds to these structname values:
//
//	go-mockgen -i Repo               structname: 'Mock{{.InterfaceName | firstUpper}}'
//	go-mockgen -i Repo --prefix Stub structname: 'MockStub{{.InterfaceName | firstUpper}}'
//
// For example, this .mockery.yml generates a fake MockStubRepo
// into the package porttest next to the interface's package port,
// like go-mockgen --prefix Stub -i Repo -o porttest/stub.port.go:
//
//	_anchors:
//	  stub: &stub
//	    template: file://.mockery/go-mockgen.templ
//	    dir: '{{.InterfaceDirRelative}}/{{.SrcPackageName}}test'
//	    pkgname: '{{.SrcPackageName}}test'
//	    filename: 'stub.{{.InterfaceFile | base}}'
//	    structname: 'MockStub{{.InterfaceName | firstUpper}}'
//	packages:
//	  example.com/app/port:
//	    interfaces:
//	      Repo:
//	        config: *stub
//
// Use different structname prefixes for outputs which share a package
// (e.g. a fake in the interface's package and another one in its internal test package),
// otherwise their names clash.
//
// # Semantics
//
// Every method of a fake has a default hook and a FIFO queue of one-shot hooks,
// both kept in the method's field (e.g. [MockStore.GetFunc]).
// A call takes the hook at the front of the queue and discards it,
// or calls the default hook when the queue is empty.
//
//   - [NewMockStore]: default hooks return zero values.
//   - [NewStrictMockStore]: default hooks panic with "unexpected invocation of MockStore.Get".
//   - [NewMockStoreFrom]: default hooks delegate to the methods of the given implementation,
//     so a real implementation (e.g. an in-memory one) can have some calls overridden.
//   - [StoreGetFunc.SetDefaultHook] and [StoreGetFunc.SetDefaultReturn]
//     replace the default hook.
//     Use them for behavior which must not change after a call.
//   - [StoreGetFunc.PushHook] and [StoreGetFunc.PushReturn]
//     append a one-shot hook to the queue.
//     Use them to override a single call: the next calls fall back to the default hook.
//   - [StoreGetFunc.History] returns a copy of all recorded calls in order,
//     each with fields ArgN and ResultN.
//     A variadic argument is recorded as a slice in the last ArgN,
//     and [StoreGetFuncCall.Args] flattens it.
//
// Calls, PushHook, PushReturn and History are safe for concurrent use.
// SetDefaultHook and SetDefaultReturn are not synchronized with calls:
// configure default hooks before the fake is used concurrently.
//
// # Not supported
//
//   - An unexported interface generated into another package
//     (go-mockgen generates a "surrogate" copy of the interface for this case).
//     Generate the fake into the interface's own package or its internal test package instead.
//   - An alias declaration (type A = I) is not an interface to fake:
//     list the aliased I instead.
//
// [mockery]: https://github.com/vektra/mockery
// [go-mockgen]: https://github.com/derision-test/go-mockgen
package gomockgen
